From 9a002032eee1f848447ee7525456bf948368a27f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] board: cargt: add i.MX 95 00414 OSM-L SOM board support

Add TARGET_IMX95_CARGT_00414 with a board port derived from
board/nxp/imx95_evk, a Cargt boot environment and defconfigs for the
00414 on the 00365 carrier and the bare osm-som.

Compared to the EVK:
 - no TCPC, FlexSPI NOR, AQR 10G PHY, MIPI-DSI splash or EFI capsule
   support
 - board_init() releases the carrier PHY resets on the pca9555
   (active-high: they drive an N-FET pulling PHYRST low)
 - ETH_B PHY management over GPIO bit-banged MDIO (i.MX 95 NETC has a
   single EMDIO controller and the 00365 wires two PHYs at address 0 on
   separate MDIO buses)
 - environment in eMMC (mmc 0), rootfs partition 1 carries boot/Image

DDR init is done by OEI and PMIC control by the System Manager, so there
is no DDR/PMIC code on the A55 side. Device trees are added as standalone
files by the recipe (files/dts).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Cargt board specific]
